Depends: libc6 (>= @GLIBC@), libstdc++6, libgcc-s1, libx11-6, libxext6, libxrender1, libxcb1, libxcb-cursor0, libxcb-icccm4, libxcb-image0, libxcb-keysyms1, libxcb-randr0, libxcb-render0, libxcb-render-util0, libxcb-shape0, libxcb-shm0, libxcb-sync1, libxcb-xfixes0, libxcb-xinerama0, libxcb-xkb1, libxkbcommon0, libxkbcommon-x11-0, libfontconfig1, libfreetype6, libglib2.0-0, libdbus-1-3, libgl1, libegl1
Recommends: libxcb-util1
Description: Control console for the Keysight 34461A bench multimeter
 A desktop console for the Keysight 34461A Truevolt digital multimeter,
 speaking raw SCPI over TCP port 5025.  It gives the instrument a
 resolution-aware readout, a live strip chart and histogram, a data log with
 CSV export, a SCPI console, and single-shot capture of the instrument's own
 screen.
 .
 The package is self-contained: it bundles its own Python interpreter, Qt 6,
 NumPy, Pillow and its four typefaces.  Nothing beyond the system C library
 and the X11/xcb libraries Qt links against needs to be installed.
